$$<p>Shri Vishwakarma Skill University (SVSU), Dudhola, Palwal, has opened applications for 45 Skill Instructor posts on a regular basis across 21 subjects. The SVSU Skill Instructor Recruitment 2026 advertisement came out on 30 October 2026, and the online form runs from 31 October at 9 am to 23 November at midnight. These are regular posts, not contract jobs, paid in Functional Pay Level 6 (FPL-6) under the 7th Central Pay Commission. The notification prints no salary figure, so this article gives none either. Computer Science and IT carry the largest share, with 10 of the 45 posts.</p>

<h2>SVSU Skill Instructor Recruitment 2026 at a glance</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Detail</th><th>What the notification says</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Shri Vishwakarma Skill University (SVSU), Dudhola, Palwal, Haryana</td></tr>
<tr><td>Post</td><td>Skill Instructor, on a regular basis</td></tr>
<tr><td>Total posts</td><td>45 across 21 subjects</td></tr>
<tr><td>Advertisement number</td><td>SVSU/2026/Estt./SI/T-37 to T-57/2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Notification date</td><td>30 October 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Apply online</td><td>31 Oct 2026, 9 am - 23 Nov 2026, midnight</td></tr>
<tr><td>Age limit</td><td>18-42 years as on 23 Nov 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pay</td><td>FPL-6, 7th CPC (no amount printed)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs 1,000 / Rs 250 / nil by category</td></tr>
<tr><td>Selection</td><td>Written test, skill test, document verification</td></tr>
<tr><td>Official website</td><td>svsu.ac.in</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>What it offers</h2>
<p>First, the nature of the job: these are Skill Instructors on a regular basis, not a fixed-term contract, not guest faculty and not daily-wage teaching. They are regular university posts.</p>
<p>Pay is fixed at Functional Pay Level 6 under the 7th Central Pay Commission. The notification states the level only, no basic pay, no starting salary, no in-hand figure, so do not trust any salary number from a job portal.</p>
<p>All 45 posts are at the campus in Dudhola, Palwal, Haryana. Subjects run from engineering and computers to German and Japanese, Music, Fine Arts and Yoga, and the health subjects of Nursing, Pharmacy, Physiotherapy and Medical Lab Technology. CSE/IT alone has 10 posts, followed by Agriculture and Medical Lab Technology with 3 each.</p>
<p>The vacancies are tentative and may increase or decrease at the time of selection. The university may choose not to fill any advertised post, and if the recruitment is not finished within six months, the posts will be re-advertised. No travel allowance is paid for any test.</p>
<p>If teaching is your line, the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/aees-teacher-recruitment-254-posts-20261028">AEES Teacher Recruitment 2026 for 254 posts</a> is another option worth a look.</p>

<h2>Who can apply</h2>
<p>The general conditions apply to every subject. You must be a citizen of India, with knowledge of Hindi or Sanskrit up to matric level essential for all posts; good knowledge of computer applications will be preferred. Age must be 18 to 42 years as on 23 November 2026, with relaxation as per Haryana government rules, and eligibility is decided as on that date.</p>
<p>Qualifications must come from a recognised board, university or institute, and experience counts only after you hold the prescribed qualification. A B.Voc or M.Voc degree is recognised wherever a Bachelor or Master degree is required. The pattern is much the same across subjects: a Master degree with 55 per cent marks plus experience, a Bachelor degree with 55 per cent plus longer experience, or a B.Voc degree with 55 per cent plus an NSQF Level 4 skill certificate plus experience. Some technical subjects also accept a first-class diploma or a trade certificate with longer experience.</p>
<p>Reservation benefits go only to candidates domiciled in Haryana; reserved-category candidates from other states are considered against General posts only. The category split is printed subject by subject in the advertisement, so check the exact category before applying.</p>

<h2>Subject-wise vacancies and eligibility</h2>
<p>The 45 posts break down across 21 subjects. The qualification shown is the shortest route the notification gives; most subjects list further alternatives.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Subject</th><th>Posts</th><th>Minimum qualification</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Agriculture</td><td>3</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs exp</td></tr>
<tr><td>Animation</td><td>1</td><td>M.Des, M.Voc, MFA or MA 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chemistry</td><td>1</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Civil</td><td>2</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Communication Skill</td><td>2</td><td>Master in English 55% + 3 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>CSE/IT</td><td>10</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Electrical</td><td>2</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Electronics</td><td>2</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fine Arts</td><td>1</td><td>Master 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>German</td><td>1</td><td>M.A. 55% + NET German or C1/B2 + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hospitality</td><td>2</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Japanese</td><td>1</td><td>M.A. 55% + NET Japanese or N3 JLPT + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mechanical (RAC)</td><td>2</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Medical Lab Technology</td><td>3</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Music (Vocal and Instrumental)</td><td>2</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Nursing</td><td>2</td><td>B.Sc. Nursing 55% + 1 yr, Nursing Council registration</td></tr>
<tr><td>Pharmacy</td><td>2</td><td>B.Pharm 55% + 3 yrs, Pharmacy Council registration</td></tr>
<tr><td>Physics</td><td>1</td><td>Master 55% + 2 yrs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Physiotherapy</td><td>2</td><td>Master 55% + 1 yr, council/NCAHP registration</td></tr>
<tr><td>Printing Technology</td><td>1</td><td>M.E./M.Tech 55% + 1 yr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Yoga</td><td>2</td><td>Master 55% + 3 yrs</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>How to apply</h2>
<p>Apply online only, through the link on www.svsu.ac.in. The form opens on 31 October 2026 at 9 am and closes on 23 November 2026 at midnight.</p>
<p>Keep your documents ready and self-attested: qualification and experience certificates, your caste or category certificate if you claim reservation, and proof of age. Every uploaded document should be self-attested and page-numbered. No document is accepted after the last date, and no change to the form is allowed after submission.</p>
<p>More than one subject means a separate application and fee for each post. Government, semi-Government or PSU employees should apply through the proper channel with a no-objection certificate; if the NOC is delayed, apply directly and submit it at document verification.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Category of candidate</th><th>Fee per post</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Male General candidates of Haryana, including DESM</td><td>Rs 1,000</td></tr>
<tr><td>General and reserved-category candidates from other states</td><td>Rs 1,000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Female General candidates of Haryana</td><td>Rs 250</td></tr>
<tr><td>DSC, OSC, BCA, BCB, ESM, EWS of Haryana</td><td>Rs 250</td></tr>
<tr><td>PwBD candidates of Haryana with 40% or more disability</td><td>Nil</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The fee is paid online only, through the link in the application form. Once deposited, it is neither transferable nor refundable nor adjustable, and the concession applies to Haryana reserved categories only. Keep your mobile number and email ID active until the process is over.</p>

<h2>How selection works</h2>
<p>Selection runs through a written test and a skill test, then document verification. The notification mentions no interview. At the first stage, every applicant sits the written test before any eligibility check. It carries 50 marks: General candidates must score at least 40 per cent, DSC, OSC, BCA, BCB and PwBD candidates at least 38 per cent.</p>
<p>Qualifiers move to the skill test, also 50 marks, with the same qualifying marks. Candidates with cumulative marks of 50 per cent (General) and 47.5 per cent (DSC, OSC, BCA, BCB, PwBD) across both tests are then considered for eligibility checking and document verification. Annexure-A gives 50 marks to the written test and 50 to the skill test.</p>
<p>The test structure and syllabus will be uploaded on the university website in due course, so check svsu.ac.in regularly. The university publishes no recruitment information in newspapers; any corrigendum appears on the website only. Marks reach candidates individually through the applicant login or by email, and objections are invited after the question paper and answer key are displayed.</p>

<h2>What the notification does not say</h2>
<p>The notification prints no pay amount for FPL-6, so no salary figure appears here. It gives no test dates and names no test centres. The syllabus and structure are promised later, with no date attached. It does not state the exact age relaxation for each category, only that it follows Haryana government rules. There is also no separate fee-payment deadline, because the fee is paid with the application itself, before 23 November midnight.</p>
<p>More large recruitments on Growentix include the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nlc-india-apprentice-1067-posts-20261026">NLC India Apprentice recruitment for 1,067 posts</a> and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/jkssb-class-iv-mts-sanitation-worker-2863-posts-20261114">JKSSB Class-IV recruitment for 2,863 posts</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> The university takes the fee only through the online link on svsu.ac.in. Anyone asking for payment for a job is running a scam. Report it and walk away.</p>

<p>Sources: Official advertisement, Ref. No. SVSU/2026/Estt./3487 dated 30 October 2026, Advertisement No. SVSU/2026/Estt./SI/T-37 to T-57/2026, Shri Vishwakarma Skill University, at https://svsu.ac.in/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Advt%20for%20Skill%20Instructor.pdf and the university website https://www.svsu.ac.in/; cross-checked with https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/svsu-skill-instructor-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-45-posts-3077463 and https://www.karmasandhan.com/svsu-skill-instructor-recruitment/</p>$$,
$$<p>श्री विश्वकर्मा स्किल विश्वविद्यालय (SVSU), दूधोला, पलवलले २१ विषयमा ४५ स्किल इन्स्ट्रक्टर पदका लागि आवेदन मागेको छ। SVSU Skill Instructor Recruitment 2026 को विज्ञापन ३० अक्टोबर २०२६ मा निस्किएको हो, र फारम ३१ अक्टोबर बिहान ९ बजेदेखि २३ नोभेम्बर राति १२ बजेसम्म खुला छ। यी नियमित पद हुन्, करारका होइनन्, र तलब सातौँ केन्द्रीय तलब आयोगअन्तर्गत FPL-6 मा छ। विज्ञापनमा तलबको रकम छैन, त्यसैले यहाँ पनि छैन। CSE/IT मा सबैभन्दा धेरै १० पद छन्।</p>

<h2>SVSU Skill Instructor Recruitment 2026 एक नजरमा</h2>
